    <DataNode elementId="AT2G28880-MONOMER" textLabel="aminodeoxychorismate synthase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8LPN3" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The protein sequence of the pABA synthase (PabA and PabB subunits) of &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; was used to isolate the cDNA encoding the aminodeoxychorismate synthase (ADCS) in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. The enzyme was recombinant expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; demonstrating the formation of 4-amino-4-deoxychorismate. Furthermore, the functional complementation of an &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; double mutant and a yeast pABA synthase deletant confirmed that the cDNA indeed encoded for a functional enzyme. The recombinant protein overexpressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; showed no ADC lyase activity indicating that the second step towards pABA must be catalyzed by a different enzyme in plants. The monomeric protein is bipartite containing tandem domains homologous to the PabA and PabB subunits of the &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; enzyme. No feedback inhibition of the enzyme was observed for neither pABA or folate which is in contrast to a closely related enzyme, anthranilate synthase |CITS: [14745019]|.</Comment>
